# =============================================
# Open Agent Builder - Environment Configuration
# =============================================
# Copy this file to .env.local:  cp .env.example .env.local
#
# IMPORTANT: This project uses a two-tier API key system.
#   - .env.local  → Only Next.js config (Convex URL, Azure AD, etc.)
#   - Convex env  → ALL API keys (LLM providers, tools, services)
# See "CONVEX ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES" section below.

# ====================
# CONVEX DATABASE (REQUIRED)
# ====================

# Get these from your Convex dashboard (https://dashboard.convex.dev)
CONVEX_DEPLOYMENT=dev:your-deployment
NEXT_PUBLIC_CONVEX_URL=https://your-project.convex.cloud
NEXT_PUBLIC_CONVEX_UPLOAD_ACTION_URL=https://your-deployment.convex.site/http/uploadFile

# ====================
# AZURE AD AUTHENTICATION (REQUIRED)
# ====================

# Azure App Registration (https://portal.azure.com → App registrations)
# 1. Create an app registration
# 2. Add redirect URIs:
#    - http://localhost:3000/api/auth/callback/azure-ad (dev)
#    - https://your-domain.com/api/auth/callback/azure-ad (prod)
AUTH_MICROSOFT_ID=your-azure-app-registration-client-id
AUTH_MICROSOFT_SECRET=your-azure-client-secret
AUTH_MICROSOFT_TENANT_ID=your-azure-tenant-id

# NextAuth.js session secret
# Generate with: node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('base64'))"
AUTH_SECRET=

# ====================
# OPTIONAL: LangSmith Tracing
# ====================
# LANGCHAIN_TRACING_V2=true
# LANGCHAIN_API_KEY=lsv2_pt_...
# LANGCHAIN_PROJECT=open-agent-builder
# LANGCHAIN_ENDPOINT=https://api.smith.langchain.com

# =============================================
# CONVEX ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES
# =============================================
# These are NOT set in .env.local. Set them via CLI:
#
#   Development:  npx convex env set KEY_NAME "value"
#   Production:   npx convex env set KEY_NAME "value" --prod
#
# --- REQUIRED ---
#
#   AUTH_MICROSOFT_ID          → Same Azure App ID as above (for backend token validation)
#   ENCRYPTION_KEY             → Generate: node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('base64'))"
#
# --- LLM PROVIDERS (system fallback - users can add their own in UI) ---
#
#   ANTHROPIC_API_KEY          → sk-ant-... (https://console.anthropic.com)
#   OPENAI_API_KEY             → sk-...     (https://platform.openai.com)
#   GOOGLE_API_KEY             → AIzaSy...  (https://aistudio.google.com)
#   GROQ_API_KEY               → gsk_...    (https://console.groq.com)
#
# --- TOOLS & SERVICES (system fallback - users can add their own in UI) ---
#
#   FIRECRAWL_API_KEY          → fc-...     (https://firecrawl.dev)
#   E2B_API_KEY                → e2b_...    (https://e2b.dev) - REQUIRED for Transform nodes
#   TAVILY_API_KEY             → tvly-...   (https://tavily.com)
#   SERPER_API_KEY             →            (https://serper.dev)
#   ARCADE_API_KEY             → arcade_... (https://arcade.dev)
#   GAMMA_API_KEY              → sk-gamma_. (https://gamma.app)
#
# --- OPTIONAL ---
#
#   CONVEX_TEST_SECRET         → For API key authentication testing
#   LANGCHAIN_API_KEY          → lsv2_pt_... (LangSmith tracing)
#   LANGCHAIN_TRACING_V2       → "true"
#   LANGCHAIN_PROJECT          → "open-agent-builder"
#   LANGCHAIN_ENDPOINT         → "https://api.smith.langchain.com"

# ====================
# SETUP INSTRUCTIONS
# ====================

# 1. Copy this file to .env.local:
#    cp .env.example .env.local

# 2. Fill in .env.local with Convex and Azure AD credentials

# 3. Set required Convex environment variables:
#    npx convex env set AUTH_MICROSOFT_ID "your-azure-app-id"
#    npx convex env set ENCRYPTION_KEY "$(node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('base64'))")"

# 4. Set at least one LLM provider key in Convex:
#    npx convex env set ANTHROPIC_API_KEY "sk-ant-..."

# 5. (Optional) Set tool API keys in Convex for system-wide access:
#    npx convex env set FIRECRAWL_API_KEY "fc-..."
#    npx convex env set E2B_API_KEY "e2b_..."

# 6. Run:
#    npm install
#    npx convex dev          (terminal 1)
#    npm run dev             (terminal 2)
#    -- or --
#    npm run dev:all         (runs both)

# ====================
# SECURITY NOTES
# ====================

# - Never commit .env.local to git
# - API keys belong in Convex env, NOT in .env.local
# - Store ENCRYPTION_KEY securely (use secrets manager in production)
# - E2B_API_KEY is REQUIRED for Transform nodes (sandboxed code execution)
# - Rate limiting is enabled by default (10 workflow executions per minute)
# - SSRF protection blocks private IPs and cloud metadata endpoints
# - User API keys are encrypted with AES-256-GCM
# - All code execution runs in E2B sandboxes (no unsafe Function() calls)
